    "debrief": "What really happened: the 2026 Iran war killed a Supreme Leader but did not topple the regime. Hormuz was closed and reopened several times, a two-week ceasefire and the Islamabad framework both collapsed, and by November the conflict had settled into blockade versus harassment, at a cost of about $47bn and 23 American dead. What experts fear: a surviving hardline regime sitting on 200-plus kilograms of 60% uranium with every incentive for a crash bomb programme, or a Gulf energy shock that tips a 3%-growth world into recession."
